  "reading": {
   "title": "Hafsa's first weeks in America",
   "text": "Hafsa made a big decision: she moved to the United States with her son Emre. They took a long flight from Turkey. Hafsa had a small suitcase, her passport and a visa in her bag. At the airport, an officer asked a few questions, and she answered them slowly.\n\nThe first weeks were hard. Everything felt strange. The food was different, and people spoke fast. Hafsa felt homesick and missed her friends in Isparta. But she was brave. She met her neighbor Linda, who brought a warm welcome and a plate of cookies. Linda gave her a map of the neighborhood and said, \"Come to my kitchen any time.\"\n\nHafsa read signs, wrote new words in her notebook and learned the bus lines. After a month she knew the city better. She found a language class and made two new friends there. Now she thinks, \"Culture and language are hard, but I can learn.\"",
